Speed alone wasn't winning this fight.

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:29.980
Also, Beerus' skill set countered many of her own attacks.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:34.480
attacks. His energy nullification, for example, let him blast through plenty of her offensive

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:40.360
options. But to really lock down Beerus' superiority in all things destruction, how about we compare

00:17:40.360 --> 00:17:45.550
their power output? Both of them used attacks that span their whole universe in seconds. But

00:17:45.550 --> 00:17:50.810
remember, the Dragon Ball universe is much bigger than our own. Right, this universe is at least

00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:56.290
nine times bigger than ours, and Beerus almost destroyed it all. For the most part, the universe

00:17:56.290 --> 00:17:59.980
Sailor Moon is very much based on our own. And the same should be said

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.180
for Nehalenia's mirror universe Usagi destroyed.

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:03.880
So, pretty clear cut?

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:06.820
That means Beerus is nine times stronger than Galaxia?

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:08.160
Well, not exactly.

00:18:08.430 --> 00:18:10.270
They both are likely much stronger.

00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:13.330
Galaxia matched Endgame Eternal Sailor Moon in battle,

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:16.380
who could destroy eight of her anima mate minions at once.

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:17.720
Did you say Animorphs?

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:19.540
Long story short, a single anima mate

00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:22.060
could match a Sailor Guardian equal in power

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:25.280
to Sailor Moon when she destroyed that mirror universe.

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:27.860
While this is admittedly a very highball estimate,

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:29.800
defeating eight anima mates at once

00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:29.980
That's cool.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:35.360
logically translate to possessing eight times that power. Since Galaxia could match her in combat,

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:40.140
this potentially puts Galaxia's output level much closer to Beerus and Goku's clash.

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:45.140
But the shockwave happened when Goku had only just gone Super Saiyan God for the first time.

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:51.280
Beerus claimed he was going all out with 100% of his power, but like all cats, he was lying.

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:56.590
Telling Goku that you were using 100% of your power was a very clever tactic to draw out his

00:18:56.590 --> 00:18:59.830
full strength, even though it wasn't true. Even after Goku

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:04.640
later achieved Super Saiyan Blue with Kaioken, a form many, many times more powerful than his

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:09.890
first go at being a redhead, Beerus was still considered his superior. Simply put, even if

00:19:09.890 --> 00:19:15.610
we highball Galaxia and lowball Beerus, the God of Destruction still possessed a greater amount of

00:19:15.610 --> 00:19:19.950
power, both in offense and defense, as they are identical when it comes to Dragon Ball Key.

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:25.350
Isn't that right, dummy? Sailor Galaxia may have had a more versatile arsenal, but Lord Beerus

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:29.970
had the strength, durability, and technique needed to overpower her. But you already said.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:37.180
all that. So what's the point? Like my existence? You could say she got caught in a galaxy-sized

00:19:37.180 --> 00:19:44.400
catastrophe. Can I blow him up this time? I look forward to it. The winner is Lord Beerus.

00:19:48.350 --> 00:19:53.910
